e] [17592186414180 1079 #uuid "3a11f4ba-4a59-5d79-a194-7e373ec165ef" 13194139534213 17592186045417 true] [17592186414181 1075 #edb/ref 17592186414164 13194139534213 17592186045417 true] [17592186414181 1075 #edb/ref 17592186414166 13194139534213 17592186045417 true] [17592186414181 1075 #edb/ref 17592186414168 13194139534213 17592186045417 true] [17592186414181 1075 #edb/ref 17592186414174 13194139534213 17592186045417 true] [17592186414181 1075 #edb/ref 17592186414177 13194139534213 17592186045417 true] [17592186414181 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139534213 17592186045417 true] [17592186414181 1077 "selection" 13194139534213 17592186045417 true] [17592186414181 1078 #edb/ref 17592186414166 13194139534213 17592186045417 true] [17592186414181 1079 #uuid "43e2c6f5-42ea-508c-b13d-901ea5805cec" 13194139534213 17592186045417 true] [17592186414182 1075 #edb/ref 17592186414160 13194139534213 17592186045417 true] [17592186414182 1075 #edb/ref 17592186414163 13194139534213 17592186045417 true] [17592186414182 1075 #edb/ref 17592186414165 13194139534213 17592186045417 true] [17592186414182 1075 #edb/ref 17592186414167 13194139534213 17592186045417 true] [17592186414182 1075 #edb/ref 17592186414172 13194139534213 17592186045417 true] [17592186414182 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139534213 17592186045417 true] [17592186414182 1077 "selection" 13194139534213 17592186045417 true] [17592186414182 1078 #edb/ref 17592186414160 13194139534213 17592186045417 true] [17592186414182 1079 #uuid "b7896c9b-7e0a-54c6-99f6-7e5e3f97a0cf" 13194139534213 17592186045417 true] [17592186414183 1068 #edb/ref 17592186414180 13194139534213 17592186045417 true] [17592186414183 1069 "q-20961" 13194139534213 17592186045417 true] [17592186414183 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534213 17592186045417 true] [17592186414183 1071 "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}2x+6y=10 \\\\ 3x+9y=21.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form, and then find the general solution of the linear system." 13194139534213 17592186045417 true] [17592186414183 1072 #uuid "2dc4858f-be36-5c29-9f4f-6c819c499765" 13194139534213 17592186045417 true] [17592186414183 1074 "First, we set up the augmented matrix for the system:\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 6 & 10 \\\\ 3 & 9 & 21\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nReducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼[\\begin{aligned}2 & 6 & 10 \\\\ 3 & 9 & 21\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 5 \\\\ 3 & 9 & 21\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 6\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x+3y=5 \\\\ 0x+0y=6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHowever, the final equation $0x+0y=6$ has no solution. It simplifies to $0=6,$ which is a false statement.\n\nSo, there is no pair $x,y$ that satisfies both equations in the system. Consequently, the overall system has no solution." 13194139534213 17592186045417 true] [17592186414184 1068 #edb/ref 17592186414182 13194139534213 17592186045417 true] [17592186414184 1069 "q-73741" 13194139534213 17592186045417 true] [17592186414184 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534213 17592186045417 true] [17592186414184 1071 "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by \n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 4 & -2 \\\\ -5 & -10 & 5\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce $M$ to row echelon form." 13194139534213 17592186045417 true] [17592186414184 1072 #uuid "66e690c7-cd96-576d-8320-9b08eb6ce160" 13194139534213 17592186045417 true] [17592186414184 1074 "Reducing $M$ to echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 4 & -2 \\\\ -5 & -10 & 5\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ -5 & -10 & 5\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+5{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534213 17592186045417 true] [17592186414185 1068 #edb/ref 17592186414181 13194139534213 17592186045417 true] [17592186414185 1069 "q-42163" 13194139534213 17592186045417 true] [17592186414185 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534213 17592186045417 true] [17592186414185 1071 "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x-3y=2 \\\\ -12x+36y=-28.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form, and then find the general solution of the linear system." 13194139534213 17592186045417 true] [17592186414185 1072 #uuid "e2f37bf7-c408-5d68-a145-8a36082b4969" 13194139534213 17592186045417 true] [17592186414185 1074 "First, we set up the augmented matrix for the system:\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 2 \\\\ -12 & 36 & -28\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nReducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 2 \\\\ -12 & 36 & -28\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+12{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -4\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x-3y=2 \\\\ 0x+0y=-4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHowever, the final equation $0x+0y=-4$ has no solution. It simplifies to $0=-4,$ which is a false statement.\n\nSo, there is no pair $x,y$ that satisfies both equations in the system. Consequently, the overall system has no solution." 13194139534213 17592186045417 true] [17592186414186 1068 #edb/ref 17592186414179 13194139534213 17592186045417 true] [17592186414186 1069 "q-42154" 13194139534213 17592186045417 true] [17592186414186 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534213 17592186045417 true] [17592186414186 1071 "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}3x+9y=12 \\\\ 4x+12y=13.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form, and then find the general solution of the linear system." 13194139534213 17592186045417 true] [17592186414186 1072 #uuid "f4b75945-9982-5318-bfc3-2aef2116e166" 13194139534213 17592186045417 true] [17592186414186 1074 "First, we set up the augmented matrix for the system:\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 9 & 12 \\\\ 4 & 12 & 13\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nReducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & 9 & 12 \\\\ 4 & 12 & 13\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 4 \\\\ 4 & 12 & 13\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-4{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -3\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x+3y=4 \\\\ 0x+0y=-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHowever, the final equation $0x+0y=-3$ has no solution. It simplifies to $0=-3,$ which is a false statement.\n\nSo, there is no pair $x,y$ that satisfies both equations in the system. Consequently, the overall system has no solution." 13194139534213 17592186045417 true]] :edb/tempids {"answer-1c7eb0bc-15c6-5831-a79d-5637e623be55" 17592186414159 "answer-1ee7bcb0-cbaf-5352-92b0-cd166136549a" 17592186414160 "answer-24a55b62-4b9f-5002-bc93-434c7062356c" 17592186414161 "answer-42e1d594-9548-59e5-aad3-072205726cc7" 17592186414162 "answer-4c9f17f4-9dc8-5361-a789-bdbc15bc853f" 17592186414163 "answer-501e28b0-b7a6-5c4a-b93c-c9142a4f1dd7" 17592186414164 "answer-584317fd-30c4-5e13-a6b5-997c0e64fc09" 17592186414165 "answer-58b4498d-2ddc-529c-be73-05b088efbf2a" 17592186414166 "answer-5995deb2-fa58-566a-aaf9-2112bbd190f6" 17592186414167 "answer-6087853b-8e40-57de-a8a4-4d62922fe815" 17592186414168 "answer-6b96e348-3bdc-514b-ab89-33c93368576e" 17592186414169 "answer-71d7b8c8-7f2d-57b3-ac13-87f27decfab8" 17592186414170 "answer-77c9e10a-76a7-504f-a64c-28abc14cbdf3" 17592186414171 "answer-80f48683-4475-5276-86de-70b5aaa6717e" 17592186414172 "a